WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.880
In 586 BCE, the Babylonians
destroy the Temple in Jerusalem.

2
00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:09.490
Many Judeans are taken
far away, to Babylon.

3
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.260
A psalm remembers them weeping
by the rivers of Babylon.

4
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.340
But sacrifice could
happen only at the Temple.

5
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.880
So without the Temple, how
did Jews keep worshipping,

6
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.470
and who now decides Jewish law?

7
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.620
In this mission, you'll follow
Jewish worship from Babylon to today,

8
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.130
and weigh what historians can prove.

9
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:33.190
Then you'll see what changed again when
the Romans destroyed the Second Temple,

10
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.010
in 70 CE.

11
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.300
Your mission: find out how Jews
kept worshipping without the Temple,

12
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.480
and who now decides Jewish law.
